  "text": "{\n  \"decision\": \"UNRESOLVED\",\n  \"issues\": [\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"TRF-010-I1\",\n      \"category\": \"SOURCE_BACKED_LOGIC_ERROR\",\n      \"source_clause\": \"1.8\",\n      \"exact_source_excerpt\": \"ships are assigned to ice classes as follows:\\n\\n      1. ice class IA Super;\\n      2. ice class IA;\\n      3. ice class IB;\\n      4. ice class IC;\\n      5. ice class II;\\n      6. ice class III.\",\n      \"exact_candidate_excerpt\": \"sh:class nltl:iceClassValue ;\\n        sh:message \\\"A ship must be assigned exactly one ice-class value. Clause 1.8 defines the controlled value set as ice class IA Super, IA, IB, IC, II, and III; canonical IRIs for those individual values were not supplied, so enumeration cannot be constrained here without inventing IRIs.\\\"@en\",\n      \"reason\": \"The shape constrains the object only to instances of nltl:iceClassValue. That does not establish membership in the six source-defined ice classes, so other iceClassValue instances could be accepted. The candidate explicitly acknowledges that the closed set is not constrained.\",\n      \"expected\": \"The representation should restrict the value to the six source-defined ice classes, subject to canonical individual IRIs or an equivalent supplied mapping.\",\n      \"suggestion\": \"Supply canonical IRIs for IA Super, IA, IB, IC, II, and III and add a closed-set constraint such as sh:in using those mapped IRIs. Do not invent the IRIs from the available evidence.\",\n      \"evidence_excerpt\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClass> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClassValue>.\\n\\\"NORMALIZED (Stage 1): candidate for iceClass derived from the linked locked requirements; scope and final semantics require vocabulary approval.\\\"@en\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"issue_id\": \"TRF-010-I2\",\n      \"category\": \"UNRESOLVED_CONTEXT\",\n      \"source_clause\": \"1.8\",\n      \"exact_source_excerpt\": \"Under section 3 of the Act on the Ice Classes of Ships and Icebreaker Assistance (1121/2005),\\nships are assigned to ice classes as follows:\",\n      \"exact_candidate_excerpt\": \"sh:minCount 1 ;\\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\",\n      \"reason\": \"Clause 1.8 states that ships are assigned to ice classes, but the supplied text does not expressly specify whether the RDF representation must permit exactly one iceClass value, nor does the ontology evidence define cardinality. The candidate's exact-one restriction is therefore not independently grounded by the supplied source and schema.\",\n      \"expected\": \"Cardinality should remain unresolved unless the governing source or an approved representation rule confirms that exactly one iceClass value is required.\",\n      \"suggestion\": \"Confirm the intended cardinality for nltl:iceClass. If exactly one value is approved, retain minCount 1 and maxCount 1; otherwise revise the cardinality constraint.\",\n      \"evidence_excerpt\": \"<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClass> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty>.\\nNo cardinality restriction for nltl:iceClass is present in the supplied ontology evidence.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"change_assessments\": [],\n  \"reconciliations\": [],\n  \"unchecked\": [\n    \"The qualitative eligibility conditions for each class—structure, engine output, navigation capability, ice severity, icebreaker assistance, steel hull, open-sea fitness, and own propulsion—are not represented by the supplied schema paths and were not assessed as enforceable RDF constraints.\",\n    \"Whether the six class descriptions are intended as independently validated classification criteria or only as controlled labels remains unassessed.\",\n    \"Canonical individual IRIs for IA Super, IA, IB, IC, II, and III were not supplied, so the required closed-set constraint cannot be completed without additional mapping context.\",\n    \"The applicability statement in section 1.1 that sections 1.8 and chapter 2 apply to all ships irrespective of year of build was not modeled because the supplied requirement is limited to clause 1.8 and the declared representation scope.\"\n  ]\n}",
